    <h2>Maine cannabis zoning FAQ</h2>
    <Faq
      questions={[
        { q: 'Is the statewide school buffer 500 feet?', a: 'No. Section 402 sets a 1,000-foot property-line buffer. A municipality may adopt a shorter distance, but not less than 500 feet.' },
        { q: 'Can I seek local authorization before receiving an OCP conditional license?', a: 'No. Section 402 bars the request, and the municipality may not accept it as complete, until OCP issues the conditional license.' },
        { q: 'Does an OCP conditional license mean my parcel is approved?', a: 'No. The municipality still must authorize the relevant establishment type and the applicant must obtain all applicable local approvals, permits, and licenses.' },
        { q: 'If a town does not respond, is the application approved?', a: 'No. Municipal silence does not satisfy local authorization. The statute provides deemed-denial and appeal procedures after the applicable 90- or 180-day period.' },
        { q: 'Does adult-use opt-in prove a medical cannabis use is allowed?', a: 'No. Medical establishments require a separate Title 22 and municipal-ordinance analysis.' }
      ]}
    />

